                <pb facs="0273" n="177" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg177"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">368.117/123: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Greece</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hall</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-07T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 7,
                                1922—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3. Your 155 December 16th, 5 p.m.</p>
                <p>When you have an opportunity bring offer of Greek authorities informally to
                    attention of interested American citizens, but avoid officially advising them to
                    apply for release from Greek allegiance. Failure to make such application cannot
                    be considered sufficient ground for withdrawal of protection.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
